L000321	
L000322	\emph{Discussion.---}
L000323	By fixing the scattering behavior at the critical energies, the universal physics discovered provides a qualitative description of the scattering behavior across a wide energy range, as illustrated in Fig.~\ref{fig:results_all} (b).
L000324	The prominent suppression of the scattering cross section is anchored precisely at the theoretically predicted \(E_{\text{sadd}}\) and \(E_{\text{max}}\), while the overall width of the interaction region is set by the natural dissipative scale of the system, \(\Gamma(\bm{p}=\bm{0})\) (here, \(\approx 6\Gamma_0\), where \(\Gamma_0\) is the single-atom decay rate). Beyond these sharp features, our results also reveal another generic property: the predominance of scattering into the dark-wave channel (\(\beta=0\)). This originates from the high density of states associated with the relatively flat dark-wave bands, which enhances the \(\sigma_{\alpha,0}\) cross section over other channels. This preferential scattering into subradiant modes is therefore a general feature of atomic arrays supporting flat collective bands~\cite{jaworowski2025laughlin}.
L000325	
L000326	
L000327	
L000328	Experimentally, two-photon cross sections can be extracted from the linear dependence of photon transmission or reflection on input intensity \cite{Wang2025MultiExcitation}. The main experimental test is to measure this cross section as a function of energy near the critical points. Although broadening due to laser resolution, finite size~\footnote{Finite-size effects impose a minimum energy resolution, scaling as \(\Delta E_{\min} \propto 1/N^2\) for an \(N \times N\) array.},
L000329	and disorder will smooth out sharp theoretical features, observing robust suppression at the critical energies would clearly validate our theory with current capabilities.
L000330	
L000331	While our analysis assumes a two-level nonlinearity and a square array, the core mechanism we identify is far more general.
L000332	 The universal phenomena arise from the singular phase space near a band-structure critical point, making the details of the short-range interaction irrelevant.
L000333	 We thus expect these universal  phenomena for a wide range of interactions and array geometries.
L000334	 The decoupling of dark spin waves from photon channels at critical energies indicates two-excitation subradiant states, discussed further in \cite{Wang2025MultiExcitation}.
L000335	This detailed two-excitation scattering analysis underpins future studies of many-body dynamics in these driven-dissipative systems.
